Error: `msgbox.askyesno.showwarning()` is invalid syntax. askyesno and showwarning are separate functions in the messagebox module, not chained methods. Fix: Use them individually:
```python
if msgbox.showwarning('title', 'text') == 'ok':
    if msgbox.askyesno('title', 'text2'):
        function()
```
Each function returns independently. Don't chain them—call them sequentially in nested if blocks.

An object is reversible if it can be iterated backward. reversed() requires either __reversed__() method or __getitem__() with integer indices. HBox (ipywidgets) lacks both. Fix: Implement __reversed__():
```python
class MyBox:
    def __reversed__(self):
        return reversed(self.items)
```
Or convert to list first: `reversed(list(hbox))`

Model collapses to predicting a constant value—common LSTM issue. Causes: (1) BCEWithLogitsLoss + Sigmoid doubles sigmoid application; (2) Loss plateaus; (3) Vanishing gradients; (4) Insufficient data variance. Fixes: Remove Sigmoid layer (LogitsLoss includes it). Verify loss decreases during training. Check gradient flow:
```python
for p in model.parameters():
    if p.grad is None: print('Dead gradient')
```
Increase dropout, use gradient clipping, or adjust learning rate.

Issue: StructuredTool doesn't bind instance methods correctly. Fix: Return bound methods or use a wrapper:
```python
def get_tools(self):
    return [
        tool(lambda path: self.read_file(path), name='read_file', ...)
    ]
```
Or use @tool decorator on wrapper functions:
```python
@tool
def read_file(path: str):
    return self.read_file(path)
```
Better: Define tools outside the class and pass self as context/state.
